import evaluate
df = evaluate.main(20, 5, seed=7)

print("""
HOW TO READ THIS
  20 scenarios each plant ONE known cause - a distributor lapse, a stockout, a
  competitor discount, or a price rise - in a randomly chosen region and month.
  5 null scenarios plant nothing, so any insight raised there is a false positive
  by construction. All 25 share the same base order book, so the only thing that
  differs between them is the planted cause.

  Top-1 accuracy is measured only on scenarios the engine actually surfaced. That
  is the honest denominator: the question it answers is "when CausalLoop names a
  cause, is it right", which is what an analyst acting on it cares about.

  Detection recall below 100% is a deliberate stance, not a defect. The engine is
  tuned for precision over recall because the failure mode the brief warns about
  is alert fatigue. Both thresholds live in kpi_contract.yaml and can be loosened
  per KPI without touching any code.
""")
